name c01m05-nights-quest
timeout 900
time 1994-10-07T19:00:00Z

# ARMORED FIST (NovaLogic 1994), CAMPAIGN ONE "OVERWATCH", MISSION 5 OF 7 — `INDIA5`, NIGHT'S QUEST.
# THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES D1-D7 are stated in full in c01m01-slaughterzone.fbm and apply here unchanged.
#
# THE TASK [FSW]: sanction the enemy FIELD COMMAND BUNKERS and the enemy COMMAND TROOP dug in on the
# encampment periphery. Course 238 SSW. Time limit 15 min [FSG], independently confirmed by
# [GUIDE p.66]'s "13 objectives in 15 minutes".
#
# THIS IS THE CAMPAIGN'S ONLY NIGHT MISSION, AND THE DATA SAYS SO ALONE. `INDIA5` is the one file in
# all 51 that loads `7.SKY` — one fifth the size of every other sky asset (14 985 B against 72-111 kB)
# and the one sky absent from the mission editor's own map table [FSG]. Its palette is `707` against
# the daylight `C07` pair the editor calls DRY DESERT PASS. 1900Z = 0000 PKT (D7); the measured sun
# elevation at the spawn point is in this run's `mission CLOCK` line and is the check on that reading.
# NOTHING IN THIS TREE CHANGES BECAUSE OF IT. `sensors/FBVisualSystem` is the only sensor with a
# daylight term, and it never sees a ground target anyway (D1); the F-16 has no thermal sight; the
# original's whole point here — "working with the thermal sights" — has no representation at all. The
# clock is a stamp on this mission, not an input. That is a named engine gap, not a modelling choice.
#
# THE 13 GOALS ARE A DERIVATION WITH ONE NAMED ASSUMPTION. [GUIDE p.66] gives the count and nothing
# gives the split; the goal flag is in the undecoded `DCBS` (campaign.md §7.4). The order of battle has
# 16 red vehicles, so goals are NOT the vehicles here — unlike mission 4, where 10 + 1 closed exactly.
# What the [FSW] task names is two things: the bunkers and the command troop. THE ASSUMPTION: the
# command troop is ONE platoon, i.e. FOUR vehicles, which is what `PINF`'s 8 slots / 4 per side and the
# manual's "up to 16 vehicles in four platoons" make a platoon (campaign.md §7.3). 13 - 4 = 9 bunkers.
# [GUIDE p.65] also names SATELLITE DISHES in the objective area, and the split of the nine between
# bunkers and dishes is NOT recoverable — so all nine carry `target_hard`, the word "bunker" and the
# pessimistic direction. Bandit 4 is taken as the command troop because it is the platoon the guide
# places on the periphery; that identification is by elimination and nothing states it.
#
# THE ORDER CLAUSE CANNOT BE JUDGED. campaign.md §6's rule for this mission is "with the rear-threat
# platoon killed FIRST — a run that leads with the forward vehicle is judged wrong regardless of
# outcome". `objective` carries no sequence in this format (doc/missions/verdict.md), and WHICH platoon
# is the rear threat is not in any source read. Both halves of that clause are therefore unjudged, and
# they are named here rather than quietly dropped.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES
#   Blue [GUIDE p.65]: Echo 1 = 3 M1A2 + 1 M3, Echo 2 = 1 M1A2 + 1 M3. SIX vehicles, six jets.
#   Red  [GUIDE p.65]: Bandit 1 (2 T-80, 2 BMP), Bandit 2 (1 T-80, 3 BMP), Bandit 3 (2 T-80, 2 BMP),
#   Bandit 4 (2 T-80, 2 BMP) = 16 vehicles, plus the nine bunkers.
#   Goals: the nine bunkers and Bandit 4's four vehicles. Bandits 1-3 are declared and are not goals.
#
# THE AIM POINTS ARE THE BUNKERS THEMSELVES. Delivery doctrine (a) puts the [FSW] task's elements
# first, and here the task's element is nine separate hardened points spread over 800 m of the axis —
# not a cluster. Five jets take bunkers 1-5 with Mk 84s; the sixth takes Bandit 4 with a canister.
# Bandits 1-3 get nothing, which is correct: they are not goals.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `m5e1a`'s UNIT_RESULT and nothing else.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires all THIRTEEN goals dead inside 900 s. TIMEOUT/exit 3 is EXPECTED: nine of
#   the thirteen are `target_hard` against a measured ~27-41 m delivery error and a 17.7 m Mk 84 fail
#   radius (D4), and four of the remaining four are half T-80.
#   THE MEASUREMENT IS THE FIVE Mk 84 `stores DELIVERY` LINES. Five independent point-target deliveries
#   against five hardened points, flown identically, is the largest single sample of this tree's
#   air-to-ground accuracy that any mod file has produced; report `aimErrM` for all five and how many
#   landed inside 17.7 m. If none did, the statement "this tree cannot kill an MBT from the air" has
#   five measurements behind it instead of one.
#   exit 1 on a blue unit is an ENGINE finding, not a mission loss (D2).

unit m5e1a
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 1
  spawn 26.06230 69.15087 930 238.0 450       # 40 km short of the encampment on the [FSW] course 238
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 25.87130 68.81220 930 450                # AIM POINT: bunker 1, the centre of the bunker line
  wp 25.75193 68.60053 1530 450               # egress 25 km down the axis
  objective kill unit m5bunk1
  objective kill unit m5bunk2
  objective kill unit m5bunk3
  objective kill unit m5bunk4
  objective kill unit m5bunk5
  objective kill unit m5bunk6
  objective kill unit m5bunk7
  objective kill unit m5bunk8
  objective kill unit m5bunk9
  objective kill unit m5b4v1
  objective kill unit m5b4v2
  objective kill unit m5b4v3
  objective kill unit m5b4v4
  objective survive

